{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S91-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4d1171f3fc1f3fd210978669615f100492fa1092050e42ecbc3b6a2bac419f49\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 calls two spoons 'our thing'; A5 protects sharing, though the relationship's survival remains implicit.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 postpones B2's contract discussion; A5 incorporates B4's separate pudding.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants contract discussion and B4 wants separate dessert, but their relationship is unspecified.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands the dessert arrangement without increasing its emotional consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies dessert spoons and B2 supplies pending business, making the encounter playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Contracts shouldn't eat alone' foregrounds a personification over A's sincere concern.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before we sign the shop over, two spoons. We always share dessert.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I ordered my own. We're allowed separate puddings.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. One shared bite first. We're selling the shop, not us.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Mine's coming in a takeaway box. My train leaves soon.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll walk you to the station. Keep both spoons out.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A protects a specific shared dessert ritual because performing it proves the relationship survives a business separation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sentimental nostalgia would value the dessert as a memory without needing to perform it now.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 says 'We still do our thing'; revised A3 explicitly separates selling the shop from losing the relationship.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative accommodates departure by relocating the ritual; S91-single-b delays departure to complete an inherited handshake.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original's emotional stakes were thin. The revision introduces a shop sale and train departure. Separate internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A3 links sharing to continuity), logic 5 (A3 accepts B2's pudding; A5 follows B4's train), relationship 4 (B2 asserts independence), heightening 4 (A5 accompanies B), specificity 5 (A1 shop sale), brevityWit 4 (A5 preserves both spoons). Total 92; spoken ABABA and word-limit gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The shop sale makes the relationship stakes clearer, but the performers must supply whether this is friendship, romance or family.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S91-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b4a118fd150077cf431a458e52c93fabba6f76b2242d9aa0b2cc74ff1ee3783b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 insists on recovering the handshake; A5 treats its shared history as grounds to preserve it.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 slows down because B2 forgot; A5 explicitly ranks the handshake above B4's waiting taxi.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 admits forgetting and B4 introduces departure pressure, giving A two distinct obstacles.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 commits to inconveniencing the taxi to complete the ritual established in A1.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's unfinished handshake is immediately playable; B4 clarifies that someone is leaving.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's comparison of the taxi's acquaintance with the handshake compresses A's relational priorities.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 88\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We haven't finished the old handshake.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I forgot the last move.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we'll slow down until your hand remembers.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We're keeping the taxi waiting.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The taxi hasn't known us as long as this handshake.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes completing the old handshake a present obligation because it embodies the continuing relationship.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General resistance to change could oppose leaving without protecting any particular shared ritual.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 works specifically to recover the forgotten move, and A5 invokes the handshake's history with both people.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The handshake version insists on completion despite a deadline; the dessert version adapts the ritual to B's departure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after a second internal reading: B2 causes patient reconstruction, and B4 causes A to prioritize shared history over departure. The original passes coach-1.0 at 88 and all applicable dialogue gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 states a priority rather than proposing a fresh practical tactic; the relational meaning depends partly on sincere delivery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S92-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c8010466d41871fa91fe65d8e86719f5f332c4d0588f896259e631a1296402c0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 treats cancelled lunch as loss of access; A5 suspects 'Keep your key' may still mean diminished belonging.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 absorbs B2's dentist into a separation sequence; A5 interrogates B4's precise reassurance.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers a mundane explanation and B4 preserves A's access, actively trying to reassure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from surrendering a key to classifying what kind of relationship the key permits.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes cancelled lunch and shared access; A5 makes the fear playable through separate key rings.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'emergencies or belonging' gives the key a concrete relational distinction without explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You cancelled lunch. Should I leave my key?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I have a dentist appointment.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"First lunch, then the key, then separate dentists.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Keep your key.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"For emergencies or belonging? I'm choosing which ring it goes on.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A converts a cancelled lunch and its reassurance into successive signs of possible permanent relational distance.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary scheduling anxiety would focus on replacing lunch rather than losing belonging.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 leaps from lunch to returning a key, and A5 fears continued access could survive only as emergency utility.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This version tests the meaning of reassurance through access; S92-single-b turns a household adjustment into feared domestic separation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal rereading: B's helpful key reassurance becomes the next expression of A's fear. The original passes coach-1.0 at 92 with a connected ABABA progression.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's 'separate dentists' is deliberately disproportionate and could sound authored if played as a joke rather than a feared trajectory.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S92-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d997f4d8d3500c21b48ee6605fa6f6d0d3b0827744b3acd0bee663f57e57534e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 treats moving a chair as preparation for separation; A5 continues fearing permanent empty spaces.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 loosely reframes B2's vacuuming; A5 scarcely uses B4's concrete offer to restore the chair.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 offers repair, but A5 repeats suspicion without making the offer consequential.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 returns to A3's empty-space image instead of developing a more specific consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's chairs and books establish a shared home, though A5 becomes abstract.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 both lean on 'spaces' imagery, reducing the sense of spontaneous practical concern.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You've moved my chair away from yours. Shall I pack the books too?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I was vacuuming.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Right. Clearing my corner first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll put it back. You can choose where.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Beside yours. Unless letting me choose means you're keeping your options open.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets a small domestic rearrangement, including an offer to reverse it, as possible preparation for permanent distance.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Territorial fussiness would object to furniture placement without predicting a relationship ending.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 proposes packing books, while revised A5 reads B's offered choice as evidence that B may still leave.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The chair version mistrusts delegated choice inside a shared home; the lunch version questions whether a retained key still signifies belonging.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision preserves the household setting and makes B4's offered choice cause A5's new suspicion. Internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A1 and A5 predict distance), logic 5 (A3 uses vacuuming; A5 uses choosing), relationship 4 (B4 grants agency), heightening 4 (A5 doubts even accommodation), specificity 4 (A1 shared furniture), brevityWit 4 (A5 'options open'). Total 90; applicable gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The game remains accusatory; A5 needs anxious sincerity rather than a deliberate attempt to trap B.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S93-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"31d528a1017f621e417a08ed51e027b519b0ac2f8b8c53017d86c25ba13862a6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 interpret receiving a familiar plate as connection, but A5 describes choosing optimism rather than finding evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's accidental plate choice; A5 answers B4 by defending interpretation in general.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects the plate story and B4 objects, but neither reply changes practical choices.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 explains A's preference for hope without increasing the claim or acting on new evidence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's chipped plate and B2's washing-up shortage establish a familiar domestic interaction.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'read into a plate' is a compact phrase but explains the game rather than developing it.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 65\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You gave me my chipped plate. We're still us, even with your bags packed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's the only clean plate.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And you gave it to me. Still looking after me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Eat before it gets cold. The gravy's separate, like you prefer.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You remembered the gravy too. I'll set your place. We can discuss the bags over dinner.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats familiar care as fresh evidence that the connection remains strong despite visible signs of departure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Protecting a ritual would require repeating a tradition; this card interprets B's existing behavior as relational evidence.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 treats receiving the clean plate as care, and A5 treats B4's remembered gravy preference as grounds for renewed company.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative builds hope from domestic care during a departure; S93-single-b uses effortless shared laughter to propose a difficult conversation over dinner.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added packed bags as explicit adverse appearances; retained the plate setting. Internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A1 and A5 infer connection), logic 5 (A3 uses B2's clean plate; A5 uses B4's gravy), relationship 4 (B4 cares while departure remains unresolved), heightening 4 (A5 sets a place), specificity 5 (A1 bags and plate), brevityWit 4 (A3 turns scarcity into care). Total 92; applicable gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 provides real affection, so the overinterpretation rests on A assuming that remembered preferences outweigh the packed bags.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S93-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4e7944645622417f8b68bb5cf72eddea31ed7c8151ce6240b0cf20cebd6c2aa9\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 treats unplanned shared laughter as connection; A5 makes that evidence justify another shared occasion.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's 'just a joke' into effortless agreement; A5 accommodates B4's need to talk.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 limits A's interpretation and B4 insists on unresolved business, preventing an uncomplicated reunion.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 converts the hopeful interpretation into a proposed dinner despite B4's serious conversation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes shared laughter, though the actual joke and reason for the difficult talk remain unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'joke's earned us a table' follows directly from A3's evidence of effortless connection.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We laughed at the same terrible joke. That's promising.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It was just a joke.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. No effort, no negotiation, still together on the punchline.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We still need to talk.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Over dinner? The joke's earned us a table.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets effortless shared laughter as evidence of connection sufficient to support another encounter.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding a difficult conversation would evade B4's request; A instead proposes a shared setting for it.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 explicitly draws relational meaning from the laugh, and A5 answers 'need to talk' with 'Over dinner?'\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Shared humor becomes a social invitation here; the plate alternative interprets practical domestic care amid a visible departure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal rereading because each correction becomes usable evidence or a new opportunity for connection. The original passes coach-1.0 at 86 and satisfies the dialogue gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The unspecified difficult conversation keeps the scene flexible but makes its emotional stakes less concrete than the plate alternative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S94-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5e19548fd72f2134db35dc899a4a78f71ce623215c16879f8660a00842c6dabe\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 accepts anger before scheduling; A3 accepts the diary's limits; A5 accepts not knowing what to say.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly answers B2's objection to a diary; A5 incorporates B4's uncertainty into the appointment.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 challenges a superficial fix and B4 reveals vulnerability, changing A's practical reassurance.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 commits to a precise time without demanding emotional readiness first.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 proposes Tuesday and A5 supplies six, although the underlying disagreement stays open.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'somewhere to happen' and A5's scheduled 'not knowing' express the same practical care economically.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We can be angry and still choose a Tuesday to talk.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"A diary won't fix this.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"No. It gives the fixing somewhere to happen.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I don't know what I'll say.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we'll start at six with not knowing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts unresolved emotion and uncertainty while arranging a concrete next opportunity for connection.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Administrative avoidance would substitute scheduling for acknowledging feelings; A repeatedly accepts the feelings and the schedule's limits.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 agrees a diary cannot fix the conflict, while A5 explicitly allows B4's uncertainty to accompany the meeting.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This version makes space for uncertain speech through scheduling; the key alternative negotiates practical access around a stated boundary.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal rereading. B4's vulnerability makes A5's appointment more accommodating rather than more controlling. The original passes coach-1.0 at 90 and all applicable gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"This is gentle character comedy rather than a large comic escalation; its specificity lies in the appointment rather than the dispute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S94-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7072447b1fbbc0b57f24e878a6ab715f92395f88c211f208175d20ca2eb20e46\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 acknowledges difficulty and offers a key, but A3's 'I know' risks dismissing B2's emotional correction.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains the key after B2's objection; A5 converts B4's boundaries into visiting hours.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 requests boundaries, but A5 defines their form without learning what B needs.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 develops the key solution into a more constrained access arrangement.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes visiting and a spare key; A5 supplies a concrete annotation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's hours beside the key economically makes an emotional concern into a practical adjustment.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I know visiting after our row feels awkward. Would a spare key help?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's not the door. I need to know you actually want me here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Fair. I'll invite you for Sunday lunch. The key can wait.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Lunch, yes. But I need to leave by two.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Two it is. I'll serve pudding at one. No negotiating with you in your coat.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A acknowledges each emotional complication and adjusts a concrete plan to make voluntary contact easier.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fixing feelings with logistics would insist that the key solves B's worry; A drops the key when B explains the real need.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 accepts B2's need for an invitation, and A5 organizes lunch around B4's departure boundary.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The diary scene welcomes uncertainty into a future talk; this scene replaces an unsuitable access solution with an invitation and a respected end time.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Clarified the existing visiting situation with a prior row and Sunday lunch. Internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A3 accepts the correction), logic 5 (A3 invites after B2; A5 schedules around B4), relationship 5 (B defines both needs), heightening 4 (A5 anticipates departure pressure), specificity 5 (Sunday lunch and two), brevityWit 4 (A5 coat negotiation). Total 95; applicable gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The revision leaves the key unused, so it no longer directly illustrates adding boundaries to key access; its practical maintenance mechanism remains intact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S95-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"107600e407a835889256697a6cce6aa8494f17eb2154d2ddc84652fba8671c12\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 selects 'for now', but A5 switches to 'too much' instead of returning to that chosen phrase.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 challenges B2's omission of 'now'; A5 uses B4's exact language, although that weakens card fidelity.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 clarifies hospitality and B4 resists interpretation, but neither adds a concrete hosting constraint.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 starts a new wording complaint rather than deepening the original phrase's implications.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a written welcome and B2 establishes permission to stay.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's suitcase metaphor is apt, but A5's 'measurement' adds another polished abstraction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your note says I'm 'welcome for now.' Should I unpack?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Yes. I meant until your flat's repaired.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then why 'for now' instead of 'until the repairs'? Is your welcome wearing out?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll cross it out. You're welcome.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"But 'for now' was there before I complained. What happens when I stop asking?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A repeatedly examines one chosen phrase as involuntary evidence of how conditional B's welcome really is.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General semantic nitpicking would move among interesting words without holding one phrase to its relational implications.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 abandons 'for now'; revised A3 and A5 both return to it, even after B offers to erase it.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This version treats a written correction as potentially concealing an original intention; S95-single-b interrogates the supposed reassurance carried by spoken 'still'.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original breaks the one-phrase requirement. Added temporary lodging during repairs. Internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A3/A5 retain 'for now'), logic 5 (A3 uses B2's repairs; A5 uses B4's erasure), relationship 4 (B clarifies and repairs), heightening 4 (A5 distrusts correction), specificity 5 (note and damaged flat), brevityWit 4 (A3 welcome wearing out). Total 92; applicable gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 can sound knowingly prosecutorial; A must sincerely believe the original wording reveals more than the correction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S95-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0ec3187a0d5beebcd559638061d64d2a325b8ff7f76ab303d8026f2e76216c5b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 selects 'still friends'; A3 resists removing 'still'; A5 questions why that same word is reassuring.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 notices B2's shortened 'Friends'; A5 directly interrogates B4's explanation of reassurance.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 affirms friendship and B4 explains benign intent, providing two different forms of reassurance.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's reassuring intention into evidence that the friendship faces a threat.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a friendship-status conversation through the precise disputed wording.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's short 'Reassuring against what' extracts the threatening implication directly from B4.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You said we're still friends. Still?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Yes. Friends.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You can't quietly remove the word after I've heard it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's a reassuring word.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Reassuring against what, exactly?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A holds onto 'still friends' and repeatedly treats its qualifying word as evidence about the friendship's condition.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fear of abandonment alone could react to any distance; this behavior depends on the exact word 'still' surviving every reply.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 notices B2 omitting the disputed word, and A5 follows B4's explanation of that word rather than changing subjects.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The spoken version questions why reassurance is necessary; the written-welcome version questions whether editing a note can erase its original implication.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal rereading because both B replies cause new scrutiny of the same phrase. The original passes coach-1.0 at 92 and all applicable gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The immediate conversational situation is clear, but no external event explains why the friendship's status came up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S96-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3a3f9784dd007978ba3ec102655bc24c860abf405a740a310d5ebb4003d78eab\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 calls repeated bakery meetings fate; A3 and A5 reinterpret ordinary causes as fate's methods.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's shared street as a route; A5 uses B4's bread as the reason fate can find B.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 give mundane explanations but offer little meaningful change beyond resisting the same interpretation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates fate's persistence without making a new commitment to continued contact.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes the bakery and third meeting this week; B2 supplies the shared street.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'efficient route' cleanly turns B2's explanation into support for fate.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 82\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Third time this week outside the bakery. Fate clearly wants us to catch up.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We live on the same street.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. It keeps putting us within talking distance.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm moving tomorrow. This is my last loaf here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\":